[
  "ACT 1: COLD OPEN & PERSONAL GROUNDING [00:00 - 03:00]\nScene: 01. Starting Soon -> 02. Monologue / Full Camera\n\nWelcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The AI Horizon & The Observable Control Plane. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 32: Chet Hendrickson & Ron Jeffries from SCNA 2013 (2013).",
  "ACT 2: SETTING THE HISTORICAL SCENE [03:00 - 08:00]\nScene: 02. Monologue / Full Camera\n\nChet Hendrickson and Ron Jeffries brought first-generation Extreme Programming lineage directly into SCNA 2013 dialogue.",
  "ACT 3: THE CORE INQUIRY: THE SOUND ABOVE [08:00 - 14:00]\nScene: 02. Monologue / Full Camera -> 04. Split Screen\n\nWhat inspired the original XP signatories when they looked at the craftsmanship movement? How did Chet Hendrickson and Ron Jeffries maintain radical clarity amidst commercialization? What principles guided Chet Hendrickson & Ron Jeffries when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
  "ACT 4: HALLWAY REWATCH & VIDEO REACTION [14:00 - 28:00]\nScene: 03. Reaction - Video Focus\n\nRoll archive footage (YouTube ID: vF-OaT-5Kqo). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "ACT 5: THE AI-ERA PARALLEL & TERMINAL WORKBENCH [28:00 - 40:00]\nScene: 05. Workbench - Code & Terminal\n\nXP practices (continuous integration, small releases, relentless refactoring) are the essential guardrails that prevent autonomous agent loops from running amok. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "ACT 6: COMMUNITY CODA, OUTRO & NEXT STREAM [40:00 - 45:00]\nScene: 08. Outro & Next Stream\n\nThank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 33. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]